# Testing & Storybook Conventions

## Unit Tests (`src/**/*.spec.{ts,tsx}`)
- **Runner & Globals**: Vitest with `globals: true` (`describe`, `it`, `expect`, `vi` are globally available) and `@testing-library/react`.
- **Theme Rendering**: Use `renderWithTheme` and `theme` (`themes.original`) from `test/utils.tsx` whenever testing theme-dependent styles:

```tsx
import { fireEvent } from '@testing-library/react';
import { renderWithTheme, theme } from '../../test/utils';
import { Button } from './Button';

describe('<Button />', () => {
  it('should handle disabled style', () => {
    const { getByRole } = renderWithTheme(<Button disabled>Click</Button>);
    expect(getByRole('button')).toHaveStyleRule(
      'color',
      theme.materialTextDisabled
    );
  });
});
```

- **Style Assertions**: Use `expect(element).toHaveStyleRule(property, value)` (defined in `test/setup-test.ts`). Note that `toHaveStyleRule` matches base class rules on the element, not pseudo-selectors like `:hover`.

## Storybook Stories (`src/**/*.stories.tsx`)
- Import `Meta` from `@storybook/react-vite`.
- Import library components from the `'react95'` path alias (which resolves to `src/index.ts`), not relative paths.
- Categorize story `title` under `Controls/<Name>`, `Environment/<Name>`, `Layout/<Name>`, or `Other/<Name>`.
- Export named story functions (`export function Default() { ... }`) with `Default.story = { name: 'default' };`.
